.\" shairport-sync-gui(1) - the AirPlay Receiver app. Installed by both the
.\" Debian and the RPM packaging.
.TH SHAIRPORT\-SYNC\-GUI 1 "November 2026" "shairport\-sync\-desktop" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shairport\-sync\-gui \- AirPlay Receiver, a now-playing window for Shairport Sync
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shairport\-sync\-gui
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B shairport\-sync\-gui
opens AirPlay Receiver, a window that shows what the AirPlay receiver in your
desktop session is playing (cover art, title, artist, album, progress, the
sending device and the audio formats) and lets you play or pause, skip, change
the volume, disconnect the sender, and start or stop the receiver.
.PP
With the PipeWire backend, the Output picker chooses where AirPlay audio plays,
and Use Device Volume, in the menu, makes the sender's volume control set the
output device's own volume. Both are saved in your settings and take effect
once no sender is connected, as the receiver restarts to apply them.
.PP
The app reads the D-Bus and MPRIS interfaces that
.BR shairport\-sync (1)
publishes on the session bus, and starts and stops the receiver through the
systemd user units
.I shairport\-sync.service
and
.IR nqptp.service .
Each user gets one window: starting the app again brings it to the front.
.PP
The app has no options of its own, but takes Qt's standard ones, such as
.BR \-platform .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/shairport\-sync/shairport\-sync.conf
Your receiver settings. Edit Settings... in the menu opens them; the app
itself changes only the output and volume settings in them.
.TP
.I /etc/shairport\-sync\-desktop.conf
The default settings, from which yours are made the first time the receiver or
the app needs them.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shairport\-sync (1),
.BR nqptp (8),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
.PP
The app's README, in
.IR /usr/share/doc/shairport\-sync\-desktop .
